Source material
---------------
The guidance in this project is an original synthesis and paraphrase of
Apple's publicly available Human Interface Guidelines, developer
documentation, design resources, newsroom announcements, and published
session videos. No Apple text is reproduced verbatim; names of principles,
pages, sessions, and API symbols are used as names. Apple's published Human
Interface Guidelines remain the authoritative and evolving source of truth:

    https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines

Factual statements about Apple products (release dates, specifications, API
names) reflect Apple's published pages on the date given in CHANGELOG.md and
may since have changed. Values marked "derived" in the text were worked out by
the authors and are not published by Apple.

Interpretation
--------------
The "philosophy" material draws on the broader design tradition Apple openly
references (the Bauhaus, Dieter Rams, Don Norman) and is interpretation, not
text published by Apple. The "psychology" material maps well-established,
independently published cognitive principles to the guidance they help explain.
These connections are the authors' own and are offered to make the guidance
understandable and generative, not as statements by Apple.

